#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0001 expect=noViolation domain=XX
#note "XX is declared a custom domain (#library custom-domain XX) so $domain_is_custom=true, and the Check's leading conjunct silences the rule even though the define's DOMAIN item carries the unpublished alias C99999 -- pins the non-custom gate. ⚠ Channel split (PLAN-codelist-terms-returntype.md P2): the real 2-letter submission values (AE, LB) ride #library codelist-terms, the NCI C-codes ride #library codelist-term-ccodes, and the codelist's own ccode/preferred term ride #library codelist-meta. Do NOT put C-codes back into codelist-terms -- feeding C-codes down the submission-value channel was the self-disarming fixture shape this replaces."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library custom-domain XX
#library codelist-terms DOMAIN LB
#library codelist-term-ccodes DOMAIN LB=C11111
#library codelist-meta DOMAIN ccode=C66734 pref="SDTM Domain Abbreviation"
#define-xml CDISC-CG0001-custom-define.xml
dataset XX
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
---
S1 | XX | 001
